From b82de41063fc95523ea4bbefd55bf9c12b8df4ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:24:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(worker): preallocate weight CUDA pool with Unmovable
 sub-O13 soak on 64 KiB UMA

On ARM64 64 KiB unified-memory hosts with iommu.passthrough=0, hundreds
of separate cudaMalloc or 2 MiB cuMemCreate allocations interleave
immortal ARM SMMU L3 page-table pages (SecPageTables) inside freshly
converted MIGRATE_UNMOVABLE 512 MiB buddy pageblocks, permanently
shattering order-13 contiguity after a single boot.

Pre-reserve one 512 MiB-aligned contiguous CUDA caching-allocator
segment sized to requested_memory minus explicit kv_cache_memory_bytes
in Worker.init_device when native cudaMalloc caching is active on a
64 KiB host with >= 32 GiB of order-13 blocks free. Soak any Zone Normal
MIGRATE_UNMOVABLE sub-order-13 blocks beforehand with a single transient
cudaMalloc (released immediately after anchoring the pool with a 2 MiB
large-pool tensor) so the entire weight pool draws from 512 MiB order-13
blocks starting at offset 0 while KV cache allocates its own single
contiguous segment without allocator-tail slack. Bypass
_scoped_allocator_max_split(20) during load_model while anchored, and
skip redundant buddy soaking in direct_loader.bind_weight_arena.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Quality: no numerical or algorithmic change; memory placement only.
Tests: pytest tests/v1/worker/test_contiguous_cuda_pool.py
       tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader.py
       tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_direct_loader_cuda.py
       tests/v1/worker/test_engine_grid_sync.py (101 passed).
Upstream-status: local candidate-63 patch.
